  &quot;notes&quot;: {
    &quot;ai_review_notes&quot;: &quot;Strong proposer (TxPipe is established Cardano infra). Catalyst Fund 14 baseline (5 protocols live) is real evidence the approach works. Concise budget (1.68M ADA total) relative to scope. Risks: (1) the agent-readiness thesis is bet-the-roadmap — if AI-agent on-chain activity doesn&#x27;t materialise as predicted, the MCP/Skills work is lower-value than pitched; (2) protocol onboarding requires cooperation from the dApps themselves; proposal lists 12 onboardings as Q1-Q4 deliverables without naming specific protocols, so there is execution risk on selection; (3) the public TRP infrastructure becomes a TxPipe-operated dependency, which is a mild concentration concern though mitigated by the open-source self-hostable design. Third-party assurance via Blink Labs is in place. Overall a credible follow-on to Fund 14 work.&quot;
