cing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fc5a8785ddd26899aaf208\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nThis proposal requests 1,308,000 ADA (plus a 327,000 ADA contingency reserve) over 12 months to deliver an open, standardized interface across Cardano's leading on-chain protocols, so any developer or AI agent can discover, integrate, and compose them through a single consistent surface.\n\nToday, there is no common interface mechanism across the ecosystem. Every integrator is forced to relearn each protocol from scratch, and rebuild the same understanding independently. This raises the cost of every integration, locks users into official frontends that may not survive a downturn, and makes cross-protocol composability impractical.\n\nThis problem is about to get worse. The next wave of on-chain activity will come from AI agents executing workflows autonomously — but blockchain is uniquely susceptible to AI slop: a hallucinated transaction on-chain can move real assets irreversibly. For…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for ongoing maintenance of Pallas, Dolos, and UTxO RPC. All contracts are on track, with milestones being…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**USD peg is not aggressive**\nPeg is conservative or neutral vs market — not requesting more ADA than spot would imply.\n\nProposals often denominate in USD at a chosen ADA price. If that peg is significantly below current market, the proposer is asking for more ADA than the same USD cost would actually require — an implicit overage. Conservative (at or above market) and neutral (within 5%) pegs are fine; aggressive pegs (more than 5% below market) are flagged.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need indepe…50:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"usd-peg-not-aggressive\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"USD peg is not aggressive\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"USD peg is not aggressive\",\"body\":\"Proposals often denominate in USD at a chosen ADA price. If that peg is significantly below current market, the proposer is asking for more ADA than the same USD cost would actually require — an implicit overage. Conservative (at or above market) and neutral (within 5%) pegs are fine; aggressive pegs (more than 5% below market) are flagged.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Peg is conservative or neutral vs market — not requesting more ADA than spot would imply.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$7a\"}]}],\"$L7b\"]}],\"$L7c\",\"$L7d\",\"$L7e\"]}]\n7f:Tdc2,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1," project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Tx3 by TxPipe: Open API Layer for C